Source: cutefish-meta
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Cutefish Remastered <remastered@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: cutefish-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
# Cutefish itself
         cutefish-core, cutefish-shell, cutefish-filemanager, cutefish-settings,
         cutefish-kwin-plugins, cutefish-qt-plugins, cutefish-terminal,
         cutefish-screenshot, cutefish-calculator, cutefish-texteditor,
         cutefish-icon-theme, cutefish-wallpapers, cutefish-gtk-themes,
         cutefish-cursor-themes, cutefish-sddm-theme, cutefish-plymouth-theme,
         fishui, libcutefish,
# Compositor: our KWin build (per-display Spaces, per-app blur)
         kwin-wayland (>= 4:6.6.6-0ubuntu0.1+cutefish1), libkscreenlocker6, xwayland,
         sddm, qt6-wayland, layer-shell-qt, xdg-desktop-portal-kde, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, polkit-kde-agent-1,
# Sound, fonts, global menu for GTK apps
         pipewire-pulse, wireplumber, pipewire-alsa,
         fonts-noto-core, fonts-noto-color-emoji, fonts-noto-cjk,
         appmenu-gtk3-module, qt6-svg-plugins, breeze-icon-theme, milou,
# Everyday apps (Firefox from Mozilla's APT repository, no snap)
         firefox, mpv, ark, curl
Recommends: cutefish-hardware, cutefish-privacy
Description: Cutefish desktop environment (Remastered)
 Installs the complete Cutefish desktop on Ubuntu 26.04: shell, file
 manager, settings, apps, themes and the KWin Wayland compositor build with
 per-display Spaces and per-app blur. Also sets up Mozilla's APT repository
 for Firefox.

Package: cutefish-hardware
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
# Kernel and firmware (stock, signed Ubuntu kernel)
         linux-generic, linux-firmware, intel-microcode, amd64-microcode,
         ubuntu-drivers-common, dkms, fwupd,
# Graphics and video decoding
         libgl1-mesa-dri, mesa-vulkan-drivers, mesa-va-drivers,
         intel-media-va-driver, va-driver-all,
# Wi-Fi, hotspot, mobile broadband
         network-manager, wpasupplicant, wireless-regdb, iw, rfkill, dnsmasq-base,
         modemmanager,
# Bluetooth (incl. audio and file transfer)
         bluez, bluez-obexd, libspa-0.2-bluetooth,
# Laptop power, charging, sensors
         upower, power-profiles-daemon, thermald, iio-sensor-proxy, acpid,
# Audio firmware for modern laptops
         firmware-sof-signed, alsa-ucm-conf, alsa-utils,
# Storage: NTFS (in-kernel ntfs3 + ntfs-3g tools), exFAT, FAT, USB, phones
         ntfs-3g, exfatprogs, dosfstools, udisks2, kio-extras, gvfs-backends,
         usbutils, pciutils,
# Printing and scanning basics
         cups, printer-driver-all, system-config-printer-common,
# VirtualBox/QEMU guests (harmless on real hardware). virtualbox-guest-x11
# only for VBoxDRMClient (extra monitors and resize under VMSVGA).
         virtualbox-guest-utils, virtualbox-guest-x11, spice-vdagent, qemu-guest-agent
Description: Drivers and hardware support for Cutefish
 Stock Ubuntu kernel and firmware, Mesa graphics and video acceleration,
 NetworkManager (Wi-Fi, hotspot, mobile broadband), BlueZ, laptop power
 management, sound firmware, and NTFS/exFAT/FAT/MTP storage support.
 Proprietary GPU and Wi-Fi drivers are installed by ubuntu-drivers.

Package: cutefish-privacy
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, cutefish-netmonitor, opensnitch, opensnitch-ebpf-modules, nftables
Conflicts: apport, whoopsie, ubuntu-report, popularity-contest, snapd
Description: Privacy defaults for Cutefish
 Every outgoing connection is checked by OpenSnitch through the Cutefish
 network monitor and incoming connections are refused and logged.
 Removes Ubuntu's crash and usage reporting and snapd, turns off
 NetworkManager's connectivity check and MOTD news, randomises Wi-Fi MAC
 addresses and disables Firefox telemetry.

Package: calamares-settings-cutefish
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, calamares, calamares-settings-ubuntu-common
Description: Cutefish branding and settings for the Calamares installer

Package: cutefish-live
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, casper, calamares-settings-cutefish
Description: Cutefish live session
 Logs the live user into the Cutefish session and opens the installer.
 Removed from the installed system by the installer.
